00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.160
- [Gary] I sure can.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:48.100
Yeah, I mean look. The good 
news  is 90% of all students

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.180
don't know what to do,
 and everybody's overthinking it.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:55.780
So what I would tell..my friend is, 
you need to really look inside your

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.340
heart and figure out what - she-

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:00.840
When you talk to yourself,
what does -she- want to do?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:05.320
I would tell you that the number one 
thing that you should focus on is doing.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:09.680
You're not going to figure this out
being in your own head.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.120
Just start doing. Do it all. 
Do some of it together.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:16.680
Mix art and bio[logy].
Mix entrepreneurship and music.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:18.040
Just  do do do do do!!

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.440
Do you understand how young you are?

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.900
Do you understand that you can
 just "do" for the next 10 years?

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.740
Do and do and do. 
Try some company for 3 years.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:34.780
Try some internship for two years.
Try some medical sabbatical for 4 years.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:39.980
You wake up from those 9 years, 
and you're 31-years-old. You're a baby.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:43.800
You're going to have a very
difficult time in getting me upset

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:48.620
or be empathetic to being crippled 
by having all these interests.

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:53.020
Put them all together. Separate them apart.  
Spend the next decade, I mean that,

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:57.580
tasting and trying. The problem is,
 you come from an environment where

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:01.420
people are going to be judging you 
if you're not succeeding in the short-term.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:04.220
And that is your vulnerability. 
The judgment of society:

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:08.980
Your parents or somebody else to-- 
as you're trying and failing

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.880
until you find your things.  
You may be lucky and your first thing

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:15.260
maybe the great thing. You may 
be lucky in your fourth thing.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.260
And I said that on purpose slowly. 
You may be lucky it's the first thing.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.980
You may be lucky it's the fourth thing.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:24.940
But you have to have the internal 
strength to be able to hold off

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:31.480
society and family judgment while you
 navigate. If you're so confused,

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:33.280
well then you need to do 
something about it.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:36.700
The answer is to do a bunch of stuff 
over the next decade to put yourself

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:41.520
in a position in your early 30s
to enjoy your world. I get that...

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:46.020
Listen,  I've been doing a lot of data
 collecting here. I understand the pressures,

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:50.440
especially in China, around becoming 
successful, so you can get your apartment

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:52.880
and start your family. I'm aware.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.640
Everybody's got pressure.

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.420
- [Yuanhao] Hi, Gary! 
After I learned something

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:04.840
about you, I am pretty
interested in how the

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.460
idea of online shopping 
came up with you

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:11.680
and made you so successful.
 I don't think only luck is enough

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.720
for such things to happen.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:18.280
Besides, how can we predict 
the future, or in other words,

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:23.300
how can we know what the 
world would be like, especially what

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.940
kind of things may be 
popular in the future?

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:30.700
Can you give us a suggestion
 on how we should think?

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.780
Thank you very much!

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.240
- [Gary] You're welcome very much.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.660
1996.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:40.854
Ebay was around.  
Amazon was around.

00:11:40.854 --> 00:11:43.360
The world hadn't accepted its upside.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:48.060
I bet on consumer behavior
 and innovation and things changing.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:50.300
So I can predict the future.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:57.080
Were there five? 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.
Were there 5 liquor stores in America

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:59.720
that had online stores 
when I launched? No.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.420
So it feels like I'm predicting
 the future, but I'm taking innovation

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:06.460
that's happening around me,
and I'm deploying it against my own

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:09.640
reality at that time.  
My bet was that we would pick

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:11.960
convenience over history.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:15.760
Because that's what humans always do 
and that's why it was so obvious.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.160
It'd be the same reason 
that I know that AI is going

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.120
to be very important.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:21.840
It's the same reason that I 
know voice is very important.

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:25.560
All the things, my friend, about 
the future, are happening right now.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.920
The question is, "Have you calibrated
how big they are going to be in

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:33.520
7 to 10 years, and are you 
looking the other way while it's right

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:36.720
in your face?" I've been 
very good at understanding

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:42.600
the arbitrages of attention and
infrastructure that drive business over

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:44.540
the last 20 years, and I
 plan on doing it for the

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:48.020
next 50 years of my life. So for me, 
I'm giving it to you right now.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.620
Whether it's using KOLs
 to drive your business,

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:57.600
whatever it may be,  right? There are 
so many opportunities out there

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:00.100
that are so black-and-white obvious.

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:02.840
Yet, we tend to look
 the other way because

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:06.900
there's no historical reference
point directly to that attribution.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:11.200
But there is. Celebrities have been 
selling products for 100 years.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:14.000
There's just new celebrities, got it?

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:18.580
So my punchline is very simply: 
The future is always the present.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:24.120
If you're guessing the future, you're guessing.
 If you're moving quickly in the reality,

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:28.240
it seems like you're predicting,
but you're just reacting.

