00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:22.700
Steve jobs wasn't able to call at 
the time, [President] George Bush, and say,

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:26.480
"You know that Facebook thing 
that's emerging? Yeah, I need that."

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:31.480
I love when... Listen, as
 you can see, my energy

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:34.000
so pro-Asia, plenty pro-China.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.140
But we can't forget that 
the "big dogs" had competitive

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:40.420
government advantages that 
created a full stack.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.540
In the U.S., it's called 
Apple, Amazon, and Facebook.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:47.380
In China, it's just all integrated.

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:53.880
Is there one more?

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:59.360
-[Skipper] There was one question from
 the guy who just left. Darren.

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:05.820
[Background chat]

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.080
-[Gary] Yeah, why don't you 
ask one. I think we're good.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.460
-[Skipper] Actually, the 
one  that I prepared,

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:12.300
I asked in the back...

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.000
- [Gary] While we're hanging out
 here having a good time...

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.480
What you're seeing, what you're 
vibing, is just a very thoughtful,

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.600
exciting moment in my career.

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:24.500
To me, looking at the 
Asian market is almost as

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:28.760
wide open and as exciting
as when I started Vaynermedia,

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.740
or when I started to get involved
involved my Dad's business with

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:34.680
Wine Library or when I 
discovered the internet or when

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:39.080
social media Web 2.0 was 
emerging from the Web 1.0, era.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.240
You've got a question?

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:42.140
- [Skipper] It's from Darren.

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:44.500
OK, go ahead. I was
 on such a good rant...

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:47.060
Nah.. I mean... Punchline being,

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:53.700
this expansion into the Asian
 market both in Mainland China and

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:57.300
surrounding marketplaces is 
going  to be a really fun frontier.

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:00.740
Go ahead.

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:03.280
-[Skipper] So this question
 is from Darren.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.220
He asked about
"How does one start

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:09.180
a process of architecting
one's business?"

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:14.220
and "When you are architecting 
your own business, how do you

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:17.320
gain support for an unpopular decision?"

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.800
"How do you convince your 
team to work on it?"

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:26.440
- [Gary] Yeah. So you convince 
your team by one of two things.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:30.520
Either motivating them through
enormous optimism or forcing them

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:35.100
through dark dictatorship.
The middle one --- The first one is

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.620
how you begin to architect 
is backwards.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:40.880
You try to figure out
 what you're doing backwards.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:42.560
You're trying to figure out 
why you're doing it and

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.380
what the opportunity is, and 
then once you understand ---

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.620
So for me, when I started
Vaynermedia. Oh, my God.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:52.564
Oh, wow, there's a lot 
of reasons why the biggest

00:16:52.564 --> 00:16:55.360
companies in the world 
don't market properly.

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:58.015
They're not smart enough?
 Not really.

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:01.120
They don't care? 
Kind of. But wait a minute.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:03.900
There are four major marketing 
companies that dictate the entire

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.840
world, and they're pushing the 
profitable items for themselves.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.780
And there's not a lot 
of talent that sees where

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:11.020
the world is going. What if 
I built a machine

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:14.640
that was so incredible at 
marketing that then when

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.500
I bought brands in the future, 
and I ran it through them,

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.720
I could take the value 
of a brand like K-Swiss

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:23.180
from $100 to $500 million
 in sales very quickly because I

00:17:23.187 --> 00:17:26.409
only did influencer marketing. 
I only did Facebook.

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:29.499
I only did...OK. Why don't 
I do that? OK.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.740
Now, the way I'm going 
to do that is I'm going to

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:33.380
build an agency that only 
sells the best work.

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:35.380
It won't be popular at first,

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.460
but I have to do it
because my long-term vision

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:42.140
requires me being the best marketer 
of the future and more importantly

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:45.600
the best at that time. OK.
I'm going to hire a bunch of kids at

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:47.960
first, because no "real" marketer
 is going to want to work for me,

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:51.120
because I'm going to tell them 
TV is bullshit and banner ads are

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:56.160
bullshit and radios are bullshit.
This is 2009.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:58.840
They don't believe in Facebook 
and Twitter, but I do.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:01.580
So let me get a bunch 
of kids and I'll show them

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:02.700
I'll teach them. 
They're fresh-eyed.

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:06.240
They don't have preconceived notions.
 Then I'll pick up market share

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:08.000
and then when the biggest
brands in the world realize

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.580
they have to use it, I'll pick
up early market share and

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:14.060
learn to....That's how you 
do it. You start backwards.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.160
I started with my ambition to buy the Jets.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.560
How am I going to do that?
Flip businesses.

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:19.840
How am I going to do that?

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:22.120
By building a machine
 around my marketing skill.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:26.160
Then getting people to 
buy-in is pretty easy,

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:30.480
and then the middle one is my 
favorite. Making unpopular decisions.

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:33.820
I only make unpopular decisions. 
DRock was an unpopular decision.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:37.140
Everybody told me that was 
super narcissistic. It's very weird.

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:40.060
The fuck do you have somebody 
following you around for?

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:43.200
And I thought that was 
probably a great idea...

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:45.120
To me, the second I feel 
a lot of push back,

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:48.800
and I actually thought of it,
and I thought it was a good idea?

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:51.120
Then I know I've got something big.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:52.860
So those are my answers.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:56.900
Do you have the self-esteem and
the confidence and the ability

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.940
to do all those things 
is a whole different story.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:02.880
Anyway, Asia is going to be good.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:06.560
Great trip and I really appreciate
everybody watching.

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:07.800
My question of the day:

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:10.300
"When you think about 
the Asian tech ecosystem,

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:12.120
- And I'll throw the whole 
kit and caboodle into it.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:14.380
Take it any angle that you want -

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.560
what are the first things 
that come to mind?"

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.160
You keep asking questions,

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:19.840
I'll keep answering them.

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:23.500
(Upbeat music)

